1
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:10,560
Qin.

2
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,880
The results are back on
that 30 years old sample

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,750
you submitted.

4
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,190
It didn't match anything on record.

5
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:19,190
Qin.

6
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,220
Zheng Ling's eldest sister said

7
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:25,300
Zheng Jing told her

8
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,980
that Zheng Ling didn't actually
build her business from scratch.

9
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:28,470
Back then, at the Little White Villa,

10
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:30,020
she found a large stash of gold bars
hidden inside the wall panels.

11
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:31,700
Without telling her two sisters,

12
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,540
she secretly took the gold bars
and used them to start her company.

13
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:35,220
Who told Zhuang Haitao all this?

14
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:37,020
Was it that Mr. Zhang you mentioned?

15
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:39,140
Mr. Zhang is even more interesting.

16
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,900
He's been using someone else's identity.

17
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:41,780
The real Zhang Jinbu

18
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:43,460
was murdered thirty years ago.

19
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,780
Someone assumed Zhang Jinbu's identity,

20
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:47,340
and that person's real identity

21
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,220
is Zhuang Haitao.

22
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,140
Zhuang Haitao?

23
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:51,380
Are you sure his name is Zhuang Haitao?

24
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,300
Zhuang... what's wrong
with Zhuang Haitao?

25
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:55,340
He used to be a construction contractor.

26
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,660
Later, he invested
in real estate and lost everything.

27
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:59,860
Then someone talked him into joining
a health supplement pyramid scheme,

28
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:00,780
leaving him heavily in debt.

29
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:01,660
I suspect

30
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,420
Zhuang Haitao

31
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,100
is the one who killed Zheng Ling.

32
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:06,940
What a coincidence. I think so too.

33
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:08,060
We looked into it.

34
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:10,060
Zhuang Haitao
and Zheng Ling's father, Zheng Wei,

35
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:10,980
used to be good friends.

36
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:12,460
I suspect Zheng Wei's disappearance

37
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:13,740
has something to do with him.

38
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:19,820
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 21=

39
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:26,780
This is all the money we raised.

40
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,980
Qian, you... You...

41
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:31,380
With things this tense right now,

42
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:32,420
Mr. Huo still dares to move the money?

43
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:35,380
It's precisely because things are tense
that we have to move it.

44
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:36,940
The banking route

45
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:39,220
is too dangerous
for anyone to touch now.

46
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:43,740
My little operation...

47
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:44,980
Wei.

48
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,420
That favor you asked me for

49
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:48,820
over drinks that day,

50
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:50,380
I took care of it for you.

51
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:52,740
Remember what you told me that day?

52
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:55,180
Qian, from now on, anything you need

53
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,580
is my business too.

54
00:01:58,340 --> 00:01:59,140
What?

55
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:00,900
Forgot already?

56
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,580
What do you want to convert it into?

57
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:06,140
Gold.

58
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,580
Use your connections to handle it.

59
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:11,620
Keep all this with you for now.

60
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:15,740
How long, and how much?

61
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,300
What about this bag?

62
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:18,620
There's 6 million in it.

63
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:19,620
And there's more coming.

64
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:23,100
Keep it all at your villa for now.

65
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:25,420
After all, Mr. Huo

66
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,980
only trusts you.

67
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:39,700
Ten percent.

68
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:40,980
I can't go any lower.

69
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:43,140
Qian,

70
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:45,340
moving this stuff around

71
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,500
means risking my life every time.

72
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:53,900
Fine. I only have one condition.

73
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,260
Don't let a third person know.

74
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:09,260
I want to make a move

75
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:11,180
on Zhao Qian's gold.

76
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,820
He's one of Huo Qicheng's men.

77
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:21,660
Huo Qicheng can barely save himself now.

78
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,140
Zhao Qian is useless.

79
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:25,900
No one will investigate if he dies.

80
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,060
What are you planning to do?

81
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:35,460
Don't you hate
Huo Qicheng and his people?

82
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:37,340
I'm giving you a chance.

83
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:38,980
Kill him,

84
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,300
and I'll give you

85
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:41,860
20% of the gold.

86
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,300
50%.

87
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,140
30%.

88
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:52,260
My store,

89
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:53,460
my villa,

90
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:54,500
my connections.

91
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:55,700
All you have to do is finish him off.

92
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:57,660
40%.

93
00:03:58,740 --> 00:03:59,740
Pay me a deposit first.

94
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:06,660
Deal.

95
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:13,980
I'll give you 200,000 upfront.

96
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:15,700
Once it's done,

97
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:17,820
I'll give you another 800,000.

98
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:18,940
When?

99
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,460
When he comes to pick up the goods,

100
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:21,820
I'll let you know.

101
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:32,060
(Zhang Jinbu)
Zhang Jinbu, from Jiangxi.

102
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,340
Two years older than you.

103
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:34,940
He looks a lot like you.

104
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:36,420
Once it's done,

105
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:38,660
you'll use his name.

106
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,860
(Zhang Jinbu)

107
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,340
You took all that money raised
from ordinary people

108
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,310
and lived it up,
doing whatever you pleased.

109
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,140
Did you never think this day would come?

110
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:07,380
You thought you could win
by turning on your own kind?

111
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:09,620
When criminals turn on each other,

112
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:11,940
in the end, someone even more ruthless

113
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,420
will devour them until nothing is left.

114
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:14,580
Greed.

115
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:15,860
Go on, keep being greedy.

116
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,060
Mr. Zhang.

117
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:12,220
Ms. Zheng, what brings you here?

118
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:13,740
Mr. Zhang.

119
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:17,420
I'm here today to discuss
a business deal with you.

120
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:19,580
What kind of deal?

121
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:21,900
My company's run out of cash.

122
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:23,340
I need some money to keep it going.

123
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:26,060
I heard you seem to have
plenty of money on hand.

124
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:30,260
How much money could
a little shop like mine possibly have?

125
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:37,180
Let's not beat around the bush.

126
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:40,420
I've known who you are
for much longer than a few years.

127
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:43,140
I saw you when I was a child.

128
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:46,700
Back then, your name wasn't Zhang Jinbu.

129
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:49,180
Dad, where are you going?

130
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:49,940
Ling.

131
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:52,500
Dad has something important
to take care of.

132
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:53,220
Once it's done,

133
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:55,100
I'll buy you a Yamaha piano.

134
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:55,540
Okay?

135
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:56,180
Okay.

136
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:59,340
Dad, I'll wait for you at home.

137
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:01,340
Bye.

138
00:07:01,910 --> 00:07:03,650
Bye, Dad.

139
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:13,500
My dad was very happy
when he left that night.

140
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,700
He said he was going
to make a big business deal,

141
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:19,220
and if it worked out,
he'd make a lot of money.

142
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,660
But he never came back.

143
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:23,620
I never thought I'd run
into you again after I grew up.

144
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:26,780
But you weren't
using your old name anymore.

145
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:27,740
Zhuang Haitao.

146
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:30,220
You took on a new identity.

147
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:36,580
Your dad made off with the funds
that were raised back then.

148
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:39,460
He must've made a lot of money, right?

149
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:42,540
Is that so?

150
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:44,020
Then have you seen

151
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,180
that rumor online?

152
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:48,020
Upstream on the Longfan River,

153
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,660
inside the Little White Villa,

154
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:52,420
there was an entire wall
filled with gold bars.

155
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,060
Those gold bars should have
belonged to my dad.

156
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:58,340
They should have been
in my family's basement.

157
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:00,060
But where did they go?

158
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:02,420
My dad got into your car

159
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:04,980
and never came back.

160
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:06,580
And you?

161
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:08,980
You changed your name
and lived on to this day.

162
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:11,500
Don't you think I have every reason
to come find you, Mr. Zhuang?

163
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:19,140
My father is still missing to this day.

164
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:20,420
Mr. Zhuang.

165
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:21,500
The three of us sisters

166
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:22,620
have no other family.

167
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:24,540
Don't you think you should help me?

168
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:26,300
I need some money.

169
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,460
Help me keep my company afloat.

170
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:30,100
I promise no one will ever know

171
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:31,980
that Zhang Jinbu
is actually Zhuang Haitao.

172
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:32,820
Do you think

173
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,180
I'd believe you?

174
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:36,500
You don't have to believe me.

175
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:40,740
Then can you tell me

176
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:43,500
where my father went that day?

177
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:51,260
How much do you want?

178
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:54,260
(Zhuang Haitao.)

179
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:55,740
(My father's disappearance)

180
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:57,180
(really does have something
to do with you.)

181
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:58,980
(I'll never
let you get away with this.)

182
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:03,340
(Zheng Ling,
you forced me to do this.)

183
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:38,540
Stop.

184
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:41,020
Why is there a checkpoint?

185
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:42,540
Did something happen?

186
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:57,820
Stop here.

187
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:08,460
Just go.

188
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:12,660
Slow down.

189
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:13,900
My dress.

190
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,020
Slow down.

191
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:17,940
You're hurting me.

192
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:19,700
You're hurting me.

193
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:20,540
You...

194
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:23,980
What are you doing?

195
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:25,460
I won't run anymore.

196
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:28,140
I won't run. Let's rest for a while.

197
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:39,420
I regret it.

198
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:41,180
Do you?

199
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:46,700
Your sister was right.

200
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:49,420
You're useless.

201
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,180
I don't have my eldest sister anymore.

202
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:52,660
And I don't have
my younger sister anymore.

203
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:54,700
I was wrong.

204
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,500
I never should've
listened to you that day.

205
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:59,220
I killed Zheng Ling.

206
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,260
I really... I was wrong.

207
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:03,220
You did nothing wrong.

208
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,620
Zheng Ling kept it
from you and lived such a good life,

209
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:09,180
while your eldest sister couldn't
even afford her medical treatment.

210
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:10,300
That's not how it was.

211
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:14,220
My eldest sister
actually knew everything.

212
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:16,140
Zheng Ling
was the smartest one in the family.

213
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:17,220
If she took the gold,

214
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:18,980
she could use it
to make even more money.

215
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:20,660
She could use that money

216
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:22,740
to give us a better life.

217
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:24,560
It was me.

218
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:26,340
I selfishly thought

219
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:28,100
she should use that money

220
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:29,580
to pay for our
eldest sister's treatment.

221
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:31,820
We were the ones
who always depended on her.

222
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:34,100
She was always helping us.

223
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:36,020
I was wrong, Zhuang Haitao.

224
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:37,940
I never should've listened to you.

225
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,100
If it weren't for you,

226
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,540
would we have ended up like this?

227
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:43,460
Would I be stuck in
this godforsaken place?

228
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:50,700
You only regret it now
that someone's dead?

229
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:52,340
It's too late.

230
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:56,900
We can't get away.

231
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:02,420
I don't want to keep making mistakes.

232
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:06,300
I don't want
to spend my life as a fugitive.

233
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:09,660
Let's turn ourselves in, okay?

234
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:15,420
Come turn yourself in with me.

235
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:16,940
Okay?

236
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:50,700
Okay. Let's turn ourselves in.

237
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:57,100
Based on information provided
by the officers at the roadblock

238
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,860
and the taxi's surveillance footage,

239
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:01,900
the two people in the car
were Zhuang Haitao and Zheng Jing.

240
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:04,380
This is the only place
in the area where they could hide.

241
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:05,980
A witness said

242
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,940
they saw a woman
being forcibly dragged by a man

243
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:10,780
into an abandoned water tower
beside the overpass.

244
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,180
(Public Security)

245
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:55,740
All units.

246
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:58,060
Zheng Jing has been found
beneath Water Tower No. 2.

247
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,420
The killer may still be nearby.

248
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:01,980
Seal off all exits
and widen the search area.

249
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:03,100
Search carefully.

250
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:05,900
Shiyu, come here.

251
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,140
Judging by the body temperature,

252
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:18,180
the victim has been dead

253
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:19,780
for no more than two hours.

254
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:30,060
There are several fresh,

255
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:32,540
tiny dark red spatter stains
on the weapon.

256
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:35,020
The pattern and distribution

257
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:36,500
of these fresh blood spatters indicate

258
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:39,340
the killer fired
from extremely close range.

259
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:42,580
That's how the blood spattered
back onto the killer's hand

260
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:44,180
and the weapon used in the crime.

261
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:46,220
The blood could belong to the victim,

262
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:47,820
or it could belong to the killer.

263
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:52,380
If the killer had a wound on his hand,

264
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:53,420
then the blood on his hand

265
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:54,820
could also be his own.

266
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:04,900
Send it for testing right away.

267
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:06,060
(Forensic Investigation Kit)

268
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:17,060
(Public Security)

269
00:15:26,770 --> 00:15:31,290
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

270
00:15:34,330 --> 00:15:39,130
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

271
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:47,210
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

272
00:15:47,730 --> 00:15:53,090
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

273
00:15:55,090 --> 00:16:03,050
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

274
00:16:03,690 --> 00:16:08,730
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

275
00:16:10,770 --> 00:16:19,090
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

276
00:16:19,090 --> 00:16:24,930
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

277
00:16:26,410 --> 00:16:34,530
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

278
00:16:35,210 --> 00:16:40,250
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

279
00:16:42,050 --> 00:16:50,090
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

280
00:16:50,370 --> 00:16:57,610
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

281
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:02,250
♪Can you hear me?♪

282
00:17:02,250 --> 00:17:06,050
♪Can you hear me?♪

283
00:17:06,050 --> 00:17:13,490
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

284
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:21,250
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

285
00:17:21,570 --> 00:17:27,170
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

286
00:17:29,050 --> 00:17:32,650
♪After all these years♪

287
00:17:35,170 --> 00:17:42,650
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

288
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:44,850
♪And tell you♪

289
00:17:46,050 --> 00:17:49,330
♪I haven't let you down♪
